  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gbelay-Geh Cassava Expansion Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Gbehlay-Geh Rural Women Farmers Multipurpose Cooperative Society initial shareholders are 90 farmers (80 females and 10 males) in (Khan Play) who currently produce gari, rice, palm oil, and vegetables as their main surplus food crop. In this follow-on expansion project, they will engage in the buying of raw cassava and production of premium quality gari for sale to the consumer on the Liberian market, particularly in Monrovia, Ganta, Sanniquelle and other major cities in Nimba County. Two grades of gari will be produced and sold, premium and coarse.,</narrative>
  </description>
